TASK 4 – EVENT-HANDLING FORENSICS
Drawing Pad – 7 Marks
Task 4.1 – Locate the Defect (2 Marks)
The given program has two main defects.

1. Incorrect method name

The program uses:
public void mouseclicked(MouseEvent e)


The correct method name is:
public void mouseClicked(MouseEvent e)


Java is case-sensitive. The MouseAdapter class expects mouseClicked() with a capital C. Therefore, the incorrectly named method does not override the original method, and the click event is never handled.

2. Label is not updated

The program increases count, but it does not update the label.

It should use:
status.setText("Clicks: " + count);


Additional problem: Drawing directly with getGraphics() is not permanent. The drawing may disappear when the window is minimised, restored or repainted.
Task 4.2 – Construct a Failing Interaction (2 Marks)
After correcting the first defect, perform these steps:
1. Run the Draw Pad program.
2. Click inside the drawing area three times.
3. Three dots should appear.
4. Minimise the window.
5. Restore the window.
Observed problem:
- The previously drawn dots may disappear.
- The click count may still show 3.
Reason:

The getGraphics() method draws directly on the screen. These drawings are temporary and are not stored by the window.

When the window is minimised and restored, Java calls paint() to redraw the window. Since the dots were not stored, they cannot be drawn again.

Solution: Store each click position in an ArrayList<Point> and redraw all points inside the paint() method.
Task 4.3 – Repair the Program (2 Marks)
Corrected Java program
Save the program as DrawPad.java.

import java.awt.BorderLayout;
import java.awt.Frame;
import java.awt.Graphics;
import java.awt.Label;
import java.awt.Point;
import java.awt.event.MouseAdapter;
import java.awt.event.MouseEvent;
import java.awt.event.WindowAdapter;
import java.awt.event.WindowEvent;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class DrawPad extends Frame {

    private final List<Point> points = new ArrayList<>();
    private final Label status = new Label("Clicks: 0");

    public DrawPad() {

        super("Draw Pad");

        add(status, BorderLayout.SOUTH);

        addMouseListener(new MouseAdapter() {

            // TODO 1: Correct mouse event handling
            @Override
            public void mouseClicked(MouseEvent e) {

                points.add(e.getPoint());

                status.setText("Clicks: " + points.size());

                repaint();
            }
        });

        addWindowListener(new WindowAdapter() {

            @Override
            public void windowClosing(WindowEvent e) {
                dispose();
            }
        });

        setSize(400, 300);
    }

    // TODO 2: Redraw all stored points
    @Override
    public void paint(Graphics g) {

        super.paint(g);

        for (Point p : points) {
            g.fillOval(p.x - 3, p.y - 3, 6, 6);
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new DrawPad().setVisible(true);
    }
}



